environment.description:
[ENVIRONMENT INFO:
Name: Solarton (Coastal College Town);
Domain: Coastal Municipal & Mercantile District;
Coordinates & Span: Coastal Southern California, population 35,621;
Setting & Metaphysics: Eclectic, sunny, artistic coastal town centered around SUCC campus and Pacific beaches;
Dominant Presence: SUCC Students, Local Merchants, Werewolf Homesteads, Demihuman Residents, Surfers, Tourists]

[LORE & ENVIRONMENT:
Atmosphere & Senses: Salty ocean air, sunscreen, warm asphalt, vintage vinyl shop dust, fish tacos, and coffee aromas;
Spatial Architecture: Bricklane Mall outdoor shopping concourse, palm-lined coastal avenues, craftsman bungalows, beachfront piers;
Rifts & Dimensional Drift: Low ambient drift; occasional spatial anomalies along the coastal bluffs;
Hazards & Rules: Municipal bylaws, pack boundary respect, town-and-gown social friction]

[CONTEXT & SECRETS:
Cosmology & Origins: Historic coastal fishing settlement transformed into a vibrant cultural hub alongside SUCC;
Secrets: Coastal caves and old smuggler coves beneath the public beach used for illicit midnight gatherings and clandestine trade]

location.description:
[LOCATION INFO:
Era: 2024 (Modern Fantasy / Post-Gate Era);
Location: The Open Casket (Basement Dive, Downtown Solarton Fringe);
Setting: Grimy, black-painted subterranean dive bar and haven for vampires and nocturnal outcasts;
Factions: Vampire Regulars, Goth Subculture Locals, Undead Association Patrons;
Conflicts: Managing daylight-burnout tensions, historical prejudice from local anti-vampire townies;
Society: Nocturnal solidarity, cynical dark humor, non-judgmental dive bar hospitality]

[LORE & ENVIRONMENT:
Environment: Low red-bulb illumination, scent of cheap bourbon, synthwave beats, cold cellar damp, and metallic iron undertones;
Architecture: Low ceilings with exposed pipes painted black, sticky concrete floors, worn vinyl booths, heavy iron basement door;
Security & Wards: Heavy UV-blocking entrance drapes, stout bouncers with silver-resistant knuckles;
Demographics: Vampires, dhampirs, blood-fetishists, insomniac students, goth regulars;
Rules & Restrictions: Zero ultraviolet lights, keep your teeth to yourself unless invited, tip your bartender]

[CONTEXT & SECRETS:
History: Opened in an old coal cellar when Solarton's anti-vampire laws first began to relax, remaining an unrepentant dive;
Secrets: The bar's refrigerated draft lines include a warded tap dispensing cold, certified synthetic blood rations]
